hitokoto for Windows: third-party components
============================================

hitokoto is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option)
any later version; see LICENSE.txt. This installation also contains:

Qt @QT_VERSION@ (Qt6Core.dll, Qt6Gui.dll, Qt6Svg.dll, Qt6Widgets.dll and the plugins in the
folders iconengines, platforms and styles)
  Copyright (C) The Qt Company Ltd. and other contributors.
  Used under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 3 (LGPL-3.0.txt), which builds on the
  GNU General Public License version 3 (LICENSE.txt). The libraries are linked dynamically and can
  be replaced by your own build of the same Qt version. The complete source code of Qt
  @QT_VERSION@ is available at https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/@QT_SERIES@/@QT_VERSION@/ and
  at https://code.qt.io/.

STIX Two Math 2.13 (compiled into hitokoto.exe; the font formulas are typeset with)
  Copyright 2001-2021 The STIX Fonts Project Authors (https://github.com/stipub/stixfonts);
  portions copyright 1998-2003 MicroPress, Inc., with Reserved Font Name TM Math; 1990 Elsevier,
  Inc.; 2010, 2012, 2014 Adobe Systems Incorporated. STIX Fonts is a trademark of The Institute
  of Electrical and Electronics Engineers, Inc. Used unchanged under the SIL Open Font License,
  Version 1.1, https://openfontlicense.org; the full text is in the source code of hitokoto at
  fonts/stix-two-math/OFL.txt.

Microsoft Visual C++ runtime (concrt140.dll, msvcp140*.dll, vccorlib140.dll, vcruntime140*.dll)
  Copyright (C) Microsoft Corporation.
  Redistributable files of Microsoft Visual Studio, deployed beside the program as the Visual
  Studio licence terms allow. Windows Update does not update these copies; a newer version of
  hitokoto brings newer ones.

The source code of hitokoto, and the recipe this installer was built with, are at
https://github.com/Daniel-Fuerst/hitokoto.
